# State Architecture Rules

## Core Philosophy

- `AsyncValue<S>` is a **data-fetching primitive**, not a UI state model
- Every screen owns a typed `ScreenState<S>` that separates domain data from UI-specific state
- Widgets **never** pattern-match on raw `AsyncValue` for full screens — only for isolated sub-widgets
- Errors are **typed and sealed**, never strings
- A screen watches **one provider** — a coordinator merges multiple async sources before the widget sees them

---

## 1. ScreenState — The Required State Wrapper

Every feature ViewModel must use `ScreenState<S>` as its state type, not the bare domain entity.

```dart
// core_state/lib/src/screen_state.dart

enum LoadPhase { idle, loading, refreshing, loadingMore }

@immutable
class ScreenState<S> {
  final S? data;
  final AppError? error;
  final LoadPhase phase;

  // UI-specific fields live here, not in the domain entity
  const ScreenState({
    this.data,
    this.error,
    this.phase = LoadPhase.idle,
  });

  const ScreenState.initial() : this(phase: LoadPhase.loading);

  bool get isLoading => phase == LoadPhase.loading;
  bool get isRefreshing => phase == LoadPhase.refreshing;
  bool get hasData => data != null;
  bool get hasError => error != null;

  ScreenState<S> copyWith({
    S? data,
    AppError? error,
    LoadPhase? phase,
  }) =>
      ScreenState(
        data: data ?? this.data,
        error: error,                  // nullable: null clears the error
        phase: phase ?? this.phase,
      );
}
```

**Rule:** `S` is always a plain domain entity or a lightweight UI projection of one. Never add `isDialogOpen`, `selectedIndex`, etc. to `S` — those go directly into `ScreenState` as additional fields on the feature's own subclass (see section 4).

---

## 2. AppError — Sealed Typed Errors

Never use `StateError(message)` or pass strings as errors. All errors must be typed.

```dart
// core_models/lib/src/errors/app_error.dart

sealed class AppError {
  const AppError();
}

final class NetworkError extends AppError {
  final int? statusCode;
  final String message;
  const NetworkError({this.statusCode, required this.message});
}

final class NotFoundError extends AppError {
  final String resource;
  const NotFoundError(this.resource);
}

final class UnauthorizedError extends AppError {
  const UnauthorizedError();
}

final class ValidationError extends AppError {
  final Map<String, String> fieldErrors;
  const ValidationError(this.fieldErrors);
}

final class UnknownError extends AppError {
  final Object cause;
  const UnknownError(this.cause);
}
```

**Rule:** `ApiError` from the data layer must be mapped to a concrete `AppError` subtype **inside the use case**, before it reaches the ViewModel. The ViewModel never sees raw strings.

---

## 3. BaseViewModel — Revised Contract

`BaseViewModel` now uses `Notifier<ScreenState<S>>` instead of `AsyncNotifier<S>`. You own the full state shape.

```dart
// core_state/lib/src/vm/base_view_model.dart

abstract class BaseViewModel<S> extends Notifier<ScreenState<S>> {
  @override
  ScreenState<S> build() {
    initialize();
    return const ScreenState.initial();
  }

  /// Called once on build. Subclasses trigger their initial load here.
  void initialize();

  /// Current domain data, safe to call from actions.
  S? get currentData => state.data;

  S dataOr(S fallback) => state.data ?? fallback;

  /// Standard guarded action wrapper.
  Future<void> runAction(Future<ScreenState<S>> Function() action) async {
    try {
      final next = await action();
      state = next;
    } catch (e) {
      state = state.copyWith(
        phase: LoadPhase.idle,
        error: UnknownError(e),
      );
    }
  }
}
```

**Rule:** Subclasses call `runAction` for every async mutation. No bare `try/catch` blocks in ViewModels.

---

## 4. Feature ScreenState Extension Pattern

When a screen needs UI-specific state beyond data/error/phase, extend `ScreenState` at the feature level — do not pollute the domain entity.

```dart
// features/dashboard/lib/src/application/state/dashboard_screen_state.dart

@immutable
class DashboardScreenState extends ScreenState<DashboardSummary> {
  final int selectedTabIndex;
  final bool isFilterDrawerOpen;

  const DashboardScreenState({
    super.data,
    super.error,
    super.phase,
    this.selectedTabIndex = 0,
    this.isFilterDrawerOpen = false,
  });

  const DashboardScreenState.initial()
      : selectedTabIndex = 0,
        isFilterDrawerOpen = false,
        super(phase: LoadPhase.loading);

  @override
  DashboardScreenState copyWith({
    DashboardSummary? data,
    AppError? error,
    LoadPhase? phase,
    int? selectedTabIndex,
    bool? isFilterDrawerOpen,
  }) =>
      DashboardScreenState(
        data: data ?? this.data,
        error: error,
        phase: phase ?? this.phase,
        selectedTabIndex: selectedTabIndex ?? this.selectedTabIndex,
        isFilterDrawerOpen: isFilterDrawerOpen ?? this.isFilterDrawerOpen,
      );
}
```

