## 7. Presentation Layer Rules

```dart
// features/dashboard/lib/src/presentation/dashboard_screen.dart

class DashboardScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final state = ref.watch(dashboardViewModelProvider);

    // Full-screen loading: only on initial load, not refresh
    if (state.isLoading) return const _LoadingScaffold();

    // Full-screen error: only when there is no prior data to show
    if (state.hasError && !state.hasData) {
      return _ErrorScaffold(
        error: state.error!,
        onRetry: () => ref.read(dashboardViewModelProvider.notifier).load(),
      );
    }

    // Render with data; refresh indicator and inline error handled inside
    return _DashboardContent(state: state as DashboardScreenState);
  }
}
```

**Strict rules for widgets:**

- `ref.watch` is allowed in `build()` only for **the single screen provider** or small, isolated sub-widgets
- `ref.read` is used inside callbacks (`onTap`, `onPressed`, `onRefresh`) — never in `build()`
- `ref.listen` is used for one-shot side effects (navigation, snackbars) — always in `build()`, never inside async callbacks
- Pattern-matching `AsyncValue` directly is only acceptable for sub-widgets smaller than ~50 lines — never for a full screen

---

## 8. Error Display Contract

Errors must be pattern-matched by type. No `.toString()` on errors in widgets.

```dart
// shared_ui/lib/src/widgets/error_display.dart

String resolveErrorMessage(AppError error) => switch (error) {
  NetworkError(:final statusCode, :final message) =>
    statusCode == 503 ? 'Service unavailable. Try again later.' : message,
  UnauthorizedError() => 'Session expired. Please log in again.',
  NotFoundError(:final resource) => '$resource could not be found.',
  ValidationError(:final fieldErrors) => fieldErrors.values.first,
  UnknownError() => 'Something went wrong. Please try again.',
};
```

**Rule:** `resolveErrorMessage` lives in `shared_ui`. No feature widget contains its own error string logic.

---

## 9. Use Case Error Mapping Contract

Use cases are responsible for mapping data-layer `ApiResult` to domain types or throwing typed `AppError`. ViewModels never see `ApiError`.

```dart
// Correct use case pattern
Future<DashboardSummary> execute() async {
  final result = await _repository.getDashboardSummary();
  return switch (result) {
    ApiSuccess(:final data) => data,
    ApiError(:final statusCode, :final message) => throw switch (statusCode) {
      401 => const UnauthorizedError(),
      404 => const NotFoundError('Dashboard'),
      503 => NetworkError(statusCode: 503, message: message),
      _ => NetworkError(statusCode: statusCode, message: message),
    },
  };
}
```

---

## 10. What Is Explicitly Forbidden

| Pattern | Why |
|---|---|
| `throw StateError(message)` in a ViewModel | Loses type info; use `AppError` subtypes |
| `AsyncNotifier<DomainEntity>` for full screens | No room for UI state; use `Notifier<ScreenState<S>>` |
| `ref.watch` on multiple providers inside a screen's `build()` | Creates fragile multi-async UI; use a coordinator provider |
| `.toString()` on `AsyncError.error` in widgets | Untyped; use `resolveErrorMessage(error as AppError)` |
| UI flags (`isDialogOpen`, `selectedIndex`) on domain entities | Pollutes domain; these belong in feature `ScreenState` subclass |
| `await` inside `build()` or `initialize()` directly | Blocks the frame; always defer with `Future.microtask` |
| `BaseViewModel` skipped for "simple" screens | Consistency across the super app is non-negotiable |

---

## Package Responsibility Map

| Package | Owns |
|---|---|
| `core_state` | `BaseViewModel`, `ScreenState<S>`, `LoadPhase` |
| `core_models` | `AppError` hierarchy, `ApiResult` |
| `shared_ui` | `resolveErrorMessage`, shared loading/error widgets |
| Feature `application/` | `ScreenState` subclass, ViewModel, coordinator providers |
| Feature `presentation/` | Widgets only — no business logic, no error string construction |
| Feature `domain/` | Entities, use case interfaces, repository interfaces |
| Feature `data/` | Repository impl, data sources — maps to `ApiResult` only |
